<section class="page-hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Build with us</p><h1>A big ambition.<br><em>Room for you.</em></h1><p class="page-intro">Better access to healthcare takes clinical knowledge, patient understanding, thoughtful engineering, and people willing to support the work.</p><p class="stage-label">Seeking collaborators, investment conversations, and sponsorship</p></section>

<section class="wrap collaboration-list" aria-label="Ways to get involved">
  <article id="clinicians"><span class="collaboration-number">01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Doctors &amp; healthcare professionals</p><h2>Help us ask the<br>right questions.</h2></div><div><p>Shape clinical workflows, specialty skills, and evaluation criteria. Help us understand what makes a recommendation useful, where uncertainty matters, and how the work fits real practice.</p><p>We’re interested in conversations across specialties and care settings.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{ site.contact }}&amp;title=Clinical%20collaboration">Discuss clinical collaboration <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
  <article id="investors"><span class="collaboration-number">02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Investors &amp; sponsors</p><h2>Back a more<br>accessible future.</h2></div><div><p>Support the work needed to turn the vision into a responsible product: engineering, clinician-led evaluation, and research into broader access.</p><p>Hipercare is not yet a legally incorporated company. We are seeking early conversations about support and possible future investment; no funding terms or commitments are offered on this site.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{ site.contact }}&amp;title=Investment%20or%20sponsorship%20conversation">Start a funding conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
  <article id="research"><span class="collaboration-number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Researchers &amp; access partners</p><h2>Bring the next step<br>closer to home.</h2></div><div><p>Explore simpler and more affordable testing technologies, practical delivery models, and the realities of reaching remote communities.</p><p>Help define research questions around feasibility, clinical quality, cost, and local needs. This work is exploratory; no testing device or field program is being offered yet.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{ site.contact }}&amp;title=Research%20and%20access%20collaboration">Explore a research partnership <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
  <article id="contributors"><span class="collaboration-number">04</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Developers &amp; open-source contributors</p><h2>Make the shared<br>pieces stronger.</h2></div><div><p>Work on the open foundations: reusable components, specialty plugins, tests, documentation, and developer experience.</p><p>HiperHealth is a concrete place to explore the architecture and find ways to contribute.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{ site.library }}">Explore HiperHealth on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
</section>

<section class="section soft-section" id="conversation"><div class="wrap split-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start a conversation</p><h2>Tell us what<br>you could bring.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>A short introduction is enough: your area of interest, the perspective you bring, and what you would like to explore together.</p><a class="button button-blue" href="{{ site.contact }}">Connect on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small-note">Our initial contact channel is a public GitHub issue and requires a GitHub account. Share a non-confidential introduction only. Do not include patient information, medical records, financial details, or private contact information.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="section wrap faq-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">A few things to know</p><h2>Starting with clarity.</h2></div><div class="faq-list">
  <details><summary>Is Hipercare already providing patient care?</summary><p>No. Hipercare is an early-stage healthcare startup. This website presents the direction we want to develop with collaborators; it is not a patient service or a source of medical advice.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Is Hipercare open source?</summary><p>The planned Hipercare service is proprietary. HiperHealth is an open-source library, and the broader approach is to build and share reusable open-source components.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Is there a company I can invest in today?</summary><p>Hipercare is not yet a legally incorporated company. We welcome exploratory conversations with potential investors and sponsors. Any future arrangement would need its own agreed structure and terms.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Do I need to work in technology to help?</summary><p>No. Clinical experience, research, knowledge of underserved communities, and support for the mission can all help shape better decisions about what to build.</p></details>
</div></section>
